  &lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400 !important; font-size: 1.3em !important; color: #000;"&gt;&lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190405/rss" title="vale.rocks" style=" color: #D94306; font-size: 1.15em; line-height: 1.25em; font-weight: 400;"&gt;CSS Curiosities of the Past&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; — A wonderful tour of the non-standard CSS quirks developers used to make browsers behave, especially &lt;em&gt;Internet Explorer&lt;/em&gt;. Covers the 'star hack', CSS expressions (JavaScript in your CSS!), IE's DirectX filters, the famous &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190406/rss" style=" color: #D94306;"&gt;box model hack&lt;/a&gt;, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
