&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;⚡️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;IN BRIEF&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190108/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;The team behind Tailwind CSS is joining Shopify&lt;/a&gt; but &lt;em&gt;"nothing changes with Tailwind CSS or any of our other open-source projects."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📑 &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190076/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;Interop 2027 proposals are open until September 23&lt;/a&gt; — you can nominate the cross-browser gaps that most need fixing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🗓️ As promised, Chrome has now &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190078/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;moved to a two-week release cycle&lt;/a&gt;, with Firefox, Edge and Brave following suit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🖼️ JPEG XL support will &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190079/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;be enabled by default in Firefox 158&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🕵️ Years ago, a developer noticed Chrome exempted Google's own sites from the setting that wipes site data on exit (Google fixed it). Now, he claims &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190080/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;it's happening again as of Chrome 152&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏛️ InfoQ reflects on &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/190081/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;jQuery 1.0 turning 20 years old&lt;/a&gt; and why it remains heavily used across the Web.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
